Found during k85 (worker). Trust requests and warnings copy source names/addresses from the (possibly cloned, untrusted) project config and git's stderr into systemMessage/additionalContext and CLI text unchanged, so control characters or terminal escape sequences could reach the terminal or the model context. Fix: one sanitizer for untrusted strings in report output (escape C0/C1 controls and ESC, e.g. JSON-style \u001b), applied in report.ts where config/stderr text is interpolated. Tests in test/report.test.ts.

2026-09-26 17:37 Started (worker). Plan: one display-safe escaper in report.ts (C0 but tab, DEL, C1, Unicode Bidi_Control, U+2028/2029, ZWSP/WJ/BOM -> JSON-style escapes), applied where report lines are built (reportText, reportHook, hooks warn, cli text builders) plus one CLI writer that escapes per line as the catch-all. Test-first.

2026-09-26 17:41 Red first: test/report.test.ts (displaySafe unit, reportText, reportHook) and test/hooks.test.ts (untrusted project source with ESC/BEL/U+202E/newline in name+path, config error naming it via warn + pending report, git's multi-line stderr, Codex rules-file problem in an evil project dir) fail for the claimed reason: raw ESC/BEL/U+202E/newline reach systemMessage/additionalContext. Also confirmed: a git failure's stderr splits one warning into 6 context lines today (k72's one-line-per-warning claim only held for one-line messages).

2026-09-26 17:45 Also found (for the skilletor board, not fixed here): (1) sources/git.ts run() passes git's stderr untrimmed, so every git failure warning now ends in a literal '\n' (before: a raw trailing newline that split the context line) - trimming stderr there would drop it. (2) config.ts accepts any source name (control characters included) while the bundle-source prompt enforces ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$; restricting names at load would reject such configs outright - a design decision. Limits left: a CLI error message is escaped per line, so a newline inside a value there stays a line break (ESC/bidi/C1 are escaped); the ttyPrompter escape is untested (needs a pty); pending reports stored by an older version are delivered as stored, once.

